    "competitor_note": "Side-by-side comparison on the identical 100,000-doc Zipf corpus and 10,000 queries against tantivy v0.26.2 (Index::create_in_ram, IndexRecordOption::WithFreqs, BooleanQuery + TopDocs::with_limit(10).order_by_score()) and an in-process uncompressed inverted-index exhaustive baseline. Zipora BMW beats both Tantivy and the uncompressed baseline on QPS@10 and p50 latency, and beats the uncompressed baseline on p99 tail latency (via peak-block threshold priming, contiguous-run Clustered decoding, and tight multi-term block-max upper-bound pruning); Tantivy v0.26.2 has ~6% lower p99 on 4-term dense-tail queries due to 128-doc SIMD bitpacking vs Elias-Fano select1 decoding. Space comparison: Tantivy's 1.227 B/posting postings figure includes doc IDs and term frequencies (IndexRecordOption::WithFreqs), whereas Zipora's 1.219 B/posting HybridPostingList covers doc IDs only and its term frequencies (1 B/posting u8) are counted in the BMW metadata bucket (bringing postings + BMW metadata to 2.375 B/posting, 1.94x larger than Tantivy's 1.227 B/posting postings); whole-index is 2.697 B/posting for Zipora vs 1.324 B/posting for Tantivy without its empty doc store (1.643 B/posting including the empty doc store)."
